// runtime/stdlib/normalization_form.kara
//
// Unicode normalization form. Carried by `String.normalize(form)`, the
// normalization-aware comparison design.md § Strings (Equality) points at:
// `==` compares raw UTF-8 bytes, so two strings that look identical but are
// spelled in different normalization forms are NOT equal.
//
// The four forms are the ones Unicode Annex #15 defines, along the two
// independent axes the names encode:
//
//   * COMPOSED (C) vs DECOMPOSED (D) — whether `é` is one codepoint (U+00E9)
//     or two (`e` + U+0301 COMBINING ACUTE).
//   * CANONICAL vs COMPATIBILITY (K) — canonical forms preserve the exact
//     character identity; the K forms additionally fold formatting
//     distinctions, so the ligature `ﬁ` (U+FB01) becomes `fi`. That is lossy
//     and not round-trippable, which is why it is not the default anyone
//     reaches for.
//
// NFC is what you want for comparison unless you know otherwise: it is the
// form the web platform, most filesystems, and most text editors emit.
//
// Prelude-visible with its variants UNQUALIFIED (`Nfc`, not
// `NormalizationForm.Nfc`), like `MemoryOrdering`'s `Relaxed` — every call
// site names a variant and would otherwise need an import for a four-value
// enum.
//
// SPELLED `Nfc`, NOT `NFC`, and design.md's Equality bullet was corrected to
// match (B-2026-08-20-41). The bullet originally wrote `s.normalize(NFC)`,
// which breaks design.md's OWN naming rule CN-4 (acronyms as words:
// `HttpClient` not `HTTPClient`, `IoError` not `IOError`) — and the
// identifier-class check enforces CN-4, so an all-caps variant name is a hard
// parse error, in the baked stdlib and in user code alike. The spec named an
// API that could not have been declared as written.
//
// DECLARATION ORDER IS THE ABI. The variants' discriminants are what codegen
// passes to `karac_unicode_normalize` and what the interpreter mirrors; the
// constants in `runtime/src/unicode.rs` and the mapping in
// `src/interpreter/method_call_seq.rs` must stay in step with this order.

#[derive(Eq, Copy)]
enum NormalizationForm {
    Nfc,
    Nfd,
    Nfkc,
    Nfkd,
}
